 "notes": "SCGS GGMS-4 Structural features map of South Carolina (Maybin, geophysical interpretation by Clendenin, 1998), 1:500,000. Named structures (shear zones, faults, Coastal Plain basins, arches, nappes) read from the map image, since the text layer holds only a few names; line types (ductile shear zone, fault, normal, thrust, geophysically inferred) are not attached per feature except where the name says shear zone. Labels that were partly hidden or ambiguous in the crops (Walhalla nappe, Laurens thrust stack, Allendale basin, Cape Fear arch, Yamacraw ridge, Eastern Piedmont fault, Millett(?) fault, Kiawah basin, Garner fault, Charlotte and slate belt labels) are not recorded. Red dots (faults located in Coastal Plain sediments) not itemized. SUBSURFACE: none.",
